{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall divide the border of your land.</b> So that they be six together with the three across the Jordan, corresponding to the six directions. And behold, the upper land is the beginning of the three borders; from there the road shall ascend and turn to the heights, and this is what it says: ״והיה לנוס שמה כל רוצח״ — 'and it shall be a refuge thither every manslayer.' For the letters of the divine name (הוי\"ה) are open and prepared for every manslayer to flee there, and there he shall find a house of refuge after repentance and the seeking of mercy, for ״טוב ה' לכל ורחמיו על כל מעשיו״ (Tehillim 145:9)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The closing citation is from Tehillim 145:9; the text writes ה' which is rendered HaShem per the transliteration rule for reverent abbreviations of the Tetragrammaton."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:24.350900618Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}